# {{name}}

An MCP server built with [`@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk).

## Quick Start

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

## Testing with MCP Inspector

```bash
npm run inspect
```

This launches the [MCP Inspector](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector) connected to your server.

## Add to Claude Desktop

{{#if (eq transport "stdio")}}
Add this to your Claude Desktop config (`~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`):

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{name}}": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/{{name}}/build/index.js"]
    }
  }
}
```
{{else}}
Start the server, then configure your MCP client to connect to:

```
http://localhost:3000/mcp
```
{{/if}}

## Adding New Tools

Create a new tool in `src/tools/index.ts`:

```typescript
server.registerTool("my-tool", {
  description: "Description of my tool",
  inputSchema: {
    param: z.string().describe("A parameter"),
  },
}, async ({ param }) => ({
  content: [{ type: "text", text: `Result: ${param}` }],
}));
```

## Scripts

- `npm run dev` — Start the server in development mode
- `npm run build` — Build for production
- `npm test` — Run tests
- `npm run inspect` — Test with MCP Inspector

